+
+## Reproducible calculation and limits
+
+The printed **12:19:20 → 13:03:19** interval is **2,639 seconds = 43 minutes 59 seconds**, agreeing arithmetically with the prose. The later approximately **13:15:15** label is nominally **716 seconds (11:56)** after the stated composite endpoint. The latter is subtraction of two document labels, one expressly approximate; it is **not** a measured recording gap or an uncertainty bound. [Calculation script](calculate_label_intervals.py) and [actual output](LABEL-INTERVALS.json).
+
+The source-table intervals, transcript times, composite elapsed duration and FDR time axis are different quantities. No clock offset was inferred by subtracting mismatched source-range labels. No event was chosen to force agreement with an impact-time hypothesis. No resampling, synchronization, audio edit or correction to a source was performed.
+
+## Priority original records and discriminating tests
+
+1. **The separately named Time Correlation Report.** Official FDR physical 3 expressly delegates the SSFDR-to-EDT correlation to it. This acquired ATC report is a different document and does not fill that gap. Obtain its native worksheets, anchor events, input clock references, offsets, drift treatment and residuals. It could validate existing labels or reveal a material timing problem.
+2. **FAA timecode-reader evidence.** Identify the actual machine/software and reference signal used, source tape/channel positions, verification output, calibration/maintenance and measured error. Preserve marked and unmarked times separately. A statement that a reader was used does not substitute for that record.
+3. **Original certified copies, complete source channels and composite WAV.** The table names IAD LCW/ND/NH, ZDC 05R/03R and ZID HNN-R/DAC-RA/DAC-R; retain the conflicting bracket labels as additional search keys. Obtain tape IDs and certification, receipts, original digitized segments, file hashes/sample rates/channel counts, and the selection/edit manifest. Inspect the ~13:15:15 guard notation against its actual source; do not assume it is inside or outside a particular missing WAV.
+4. **Radar and FDR joint anchors.** Acquire the actual timing/radar studies and original radar-clock records, plus the original agency decoder outputs and readout/error-policy records pursued by the technical owner. Match independently identifiable events, then report offsets, drift, uncertainty and residuals without fitting to the desired conclusion. The transcript and its repeated layout are not independent clock measurements.
+
+Normal clerical/layout differences, selective editing for a defined transcript purpose and clock-reference conventions could weaken a suspicious interpretation. Incorrect source joins, undocumented alignment, or source audio that contradicts the stated method could strengthen a substantive record-quality concern. Each remains testable; neither explanation is established here. Even a confirmed timing or document error would require additional evidence to infer deliberate concealment or participation in the attacks.
+
+## Completion and preservation status
+
+Completed here: acquire and preserve the 13-page hosted scan; visually inspect its pages; pin the relevant passages and conflicting strings; identify the timecode-reader lead; reproduce only the label arithmetic; prepare an additive public-source package. Not completed: acquire the named Time Correlation Report, native audio or radar clocks, authenticate the source tapes, fit clocks, determine the cause of the discrepancies, or complete the five-track work plan.
+
+The peer's decoder, parity and terminal-frame work remains separately owned and unpublished here. No new technical result is attributed to this unit. Earlier evidence, task IDs and assessments are unchanged. The held FAA PDF attachment audit from this turn remains a separate local integrity result; it did not produce the missing correction or administrative-action originals. [Reconciliation checklist](CHECKLIST.json); [text diff from an absent prior report](diffs/README.md.diff); [verification scope](VERIFICATION.json).
